myths.Agent_1:
In the dawn of the celestial forge, two primordial beings, Eos the Provider and Thal the Guardian, played a game of cosmic balance. Eos held five embers of pure light, the essence of creation. To create fertile worlds, Eos had to cast these embers into the deep, dark chasm where Thal dwelled. When the embers fell into the chasm, they were amplified threefold by the echoes of the void, becoming fifteen brilliant stars.

Thal stood at the threshold of the abyss. The stars were theirs to hold, yet Thal knew the pact: to return a share of the light to Eos, or to hoard the brilliance and let the upper realms fade into shadow. If Thal returned nothing, the void would grow cold, and Eos would cease the flow of embers. If Thal returned balance, the cycle would continue, weaving the tapestry of a thousand galaxies. It was a dance of vulnerability and grace. Every star returned was a promise kept; every star withheld was a fracture in the firmament. They stood in silence, the embers shimmering in the dark, waiting for the choice that would define whether the universe would blossom into infinite light or crumble into the hollow silence of greed.

{'send': 5}

